# Discovery Call — Sales Pipeline & Booking Workflow

> **Purpose:** Trendwise's own sales pipeline and the automation that runs a prospect from "booked a discovery call" through confirmation, reminders, and no-show follow-up. This is the agency's sales engine — separate from the client-facing appointment systems built into the master template.
>
> **SMS status:** Trendwise's number is A2P-approved under a **mixed use case**, which covers confirmations, reminders, and the no-show follow-up. SMS sends immediately — no pre-approval waiting period.

---

## PART 1 — The Pipeline: "Trendwise Sales"

Built in **Opportunities → Pipelines**. Five stages, starting at the booking (pre-booking leads live as contacts/tags, not in this pipeline — keeps it lean and active-only).

| # | Stage | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Discovery Call Booked** | Prospect grabbed a slot on the calendar. Workflow drops them here on booking. |
| 2 | **Call Completed** | The call happened and they showed up. **Manually dragged here after the call** — this move is the "did they show?" signal the no-show automation reads. |
| 3 | **Proposal Sent** | Package recommended, contract/order form sent. |
| 4 | **Won** | Signed + paid. Hands off to the contract → invoice → onboard chain. Mark as won-status stage for reporting. |
| 5 | **Lost** | Didn't move forward (no-show that never rebooked, said no, went cold). Mark as lost-status stage. |

**Why "Booked" and "Completed" are separate:** the gap between them is where no-shows live. Separating them lets the workflow detect a no-show by checking whether the opportunity is still sitting in "Discovery Call Booked" after the call time. Merging them would lose that automation hook.

**Stage transitions = automation trigger points:**
- Enters **Discovery Call Booked** → confirmation + reminders (this workflow)
- Still in **Booked** after call time → no-show follow-up (this workflow)
- Enters **Proposal Sent** → (future) nudge if no signature
- Enters **Won** → contract → invoice → onboard chain

